  "text": "25. Myanmar has made a reservation to Article VIII of the Genocide Convention to restrict the\ncompetent organs of the UN to take actions under the Charter of the UN as they consider\nappropriate for the prevention and suppression of acts of genocide. Myanmar claims that\nsince ICJ is the principal organ of the UN, there is a limitation on Article IX. The claim is:\n(A) Maintainable, as the reservation explicitly prohibits the intervention of UN organs.\n(B) Not maintainable, as Article VIIl concerns the discretionary function which is different\nfrom the judicial function of the ICJ.\n(C) Maintainable, as the two provisions of the treaty i.e., Article VIII and IX are to be interpreted\nharmoniously.\n(D) Not maintainable, as ICJ as a successor of PClJ is regulated by the Statute of ICJU and\nnot the UN Charter.",
